; TEMPLATE ONLY. MTN must provide the real host, port, transport, IP/auth model,
; allowed codecs, source-IP policy, and number format before these sections are
; copied into the live PJSIP configuration. Never invent values in this file.
;
; Define a provider-facing transport bound only to the PBX's intended private or
; provider-approved interface. Do not reuse the loopback-only test transport.
;
; Authenticated SIP trunk pattern (replace every angle-bracket value privately):
; [mcare-provider-auth]
; type=auth
; auth_type=userpass
; username=<MTN-provided-username>
; password=<MTN-provided-secret>
;
; [mcare-provider-aor]
; type=aor
; contact=sip:<MTN-provided-SIP-host>:<MTN-provided-port>
;
; [mcare-mtn]
; type=endpoint
; transport=<provider-facing-transport-name>
; context=mcare-deny-inbound
; disallow=all
; allow=<MTN-approved-codec-list>
; outbound_auth=mcare-provider-auth
; aors=mcare-provider-aor
; direct_media=no
; rtp_symmetric=yes
; force_rport=yes
; rewrite_contact=yes
;
; If MTN requires REGISTER-based authentication, use a registration object with
; the exact server_uri/client_uri/expiration values they supply. If MTN uses
; source-IP authentication, omit outbound_auth and configure identify/match only
; for the exact provider source addresses. Do not enable both patterns by guess.
